{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters","id":1513057,"title":"How do you deal with 'invincible' characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-28T03:53:48-07:00","id":1513057,"title":"How do you deal with 'invincible' characters?","content":"So some combinations of powers make individuals virtually unkillable and yet they remain super dangerous. How do you deal with that? Claws, fangs and burning blade work on everything? Wards? The enemy mysteriously getting a shipment of holy hand grenades and sunlight bombs? Do you see nigh-invincible characters as a bug or a feature? <br /> <br /> <b>Mist form + damaging thaumaturgy</b><br /> <b>Incorporeal passage + damaging thaumaturgy</b> or mental disciplines. <br /> <b>Elemental mastery</b> (turn yourself into a small steel statue or ball with power 4, animate yourself with 3. With such dense steel, you should be virtually impervious to the bulk of small arms. Also, as far as I know, there's no rules for how damage to your form relates to your health) Even if we decide on rules like &quot;well you're steel but given your size we should reduce your strength to 1&quot; there's still things like being allowed to use Potence in the new form. <br /> <b>Bloodform+Acid blood</b> (+ fire immunity.) <br /> <br /> Also, <b>Donning the Mask of Shadows</b> RAW won't end when you attack or interact with the world, so while you're not truly invincible it could be said that this power lets you breeze through everything except for very specialized preparations (which most characters won't reasonably have, unless the ST is being a dick) Not to mention you can use this power on the rest of your coterie. perhaps something like a bloodstain on the weapon could be a still-difficult to spot giveaway, but even then you'd have to consider things like blind fighting rules..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T04:43:15-07:00","id":1513060,"title":"","content":"Never had players who attempted som invulnerable combinations. The closest is shadow form and arms of Ahriman, that comes naturally provided from Obtenebroken. Mostly seen blood form as an escape tool. <br /> <br /> The normal vulnerabilities still remain. Auspex allows someone to predict an assault. Presence has three different powers that end fights, animalism has two. It is a threat that Potence/Celerity cannot easily solve, but that might be a good thing?<br /> <br /> it has been ages since I read/played preV5, but any shapeshifter power did state what disciples were kept in a new shape/body, so unless written out, I do not think anything follows over to the metal statue. But perhaps it gives a better explanation than I did, so that might be moot!<br /> <br /> As for donning the mask of shadows, that depends on version. The one I googled up clearly states that it breaks as if by Obfuscate rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T05:17:20-07:00","id":1513061,"title":"","content":"It is a feature for me. Sometimes the world just isn't fair. Take for example, straight from VTM 1st Edition Player's Guide.<br /> &quot;There is something of a sadistic side to all this. In most Chronicles no player will ever come near to having a 10th level discipline, yet we list the 10th level powers to all the disciplines. For more than any other reason, we want to make you much more aware of what you might be going up against. You are indeed a creature of considerable power, <b>but your elders are even more powerful, and that fact you must never forget</b>.&quot;<br /> If you face a 600-year-old Elder with 40+ discipline powers, most of them 6th or 7th dot, and a bunch more combination disciplines that's just how it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T05:20:06-07:00","id":1513062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trassel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters?p=1513060#post1513060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never had players who attempted som invulnerable combinations. The closest is shadow form and arms of Ahriman, that comes naturally provided from Obtenebroken. Mostly seen blood form as an escape tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought of Shadow Form and arms, however, some people have suggested you can't do that RAW since shadow form says you can only use &quot;mental&quot; disciplines, which usually means Dominate and dementation. I think is a little strange since mist form doesn't have that penalty (Though it doesn't let you Dominate while being a shadow does?) However, it does say &quot;she may not <i>herself</i> attack&quot; which is very specific and maybe a suggestion that the Arms could attack.<br /> Some write ups of tentacles have blood spurt out of the vampire into little puddles from which tentacles emerge. Can tenebrous form bleed? That's not the case for 20th.<br /> <br /> It gets even more dangerous if you combine it with Abyss mysticism (Feed through tentacles: Never be in human form again!) and Diamonion 6 or an infernal investment for fire immunity (not entirely unreasonable given the bloodline that uses both) you're basically only vulnerable to direct magical damage, faith and sunlight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it has been ages since I read/played preV5, but any shapeshifter power did state what disciples were kept in a new shape/body, so unless written out, I do not think anything follows over to the metal statue. But perhaps it gives a better explanation than I did, so that might be moot! </div> </div> </div>In 20th, you get everything so long as you get at least 3 successes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for donning the mask of shadows, that depends on version. The one I googled up clearly states that it breaks as if by Obfuscate rules. </div> </div> </div>Googling stuff up usually gets you house rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T09:20:09-07:00","id":1513083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters#post1513057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So some combinations of powers make individuals virtually unkillable and yet they remain super dangerous. How do you deal with that? Claws, fangs and burning blade work on everything? Wards? The enemy mysteriously getting a shipment of holy hand grenades and sunlight bombs? Do you see nigh-invincible characters as a bug or a feature?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is damn hard to build such a PC<br /> I mean a ST could sesne miles away, you are planning to do something like that, and to reach that combinaton of disciplines you described takes time - godd luck to have protean AND thaumaturgy on such high level<br /> Enough to &quot;convince&quot; the said player, Vampire is not D&amp;D, it is not about power and most often than not, the power itself what destroys you<br /> But of course it is ultimately depends of the game. If the ST allows such thing or the players want to be immortal blood goods with cool powers to massacre a whole town? The point of the game is to have fun after all, you don't need a solution to something that is not a problem in your game<br /> IF the ST never intended them to have such things and it destructive and distruptive to the Chronicle? The ST always could use the &quot;bigger fish&quot; method; &quot;So you belive you are the big fish in your little pond amigo? Sure... but your splish plash in the water attracts attention, the attention of sharks. Hungry and powerfull sharks&quot;<br /> It comes down to the question, you re asking it as a Player or as a Storyteller?<br /> If as Player? The enemy with such power setup was made by the ST for a <i>reason </i>usually a hint, brute force is not enough, you have to use your brain, creativity, manipulation, byzantine politics, machiavellian methods, web of boons and favors and so on... IF one of your packmate became such entity with powers? A bit similar. The ST let the player to achieve that for a <i>reason</i><br /> And usually it is not a good sign... (actually a very very very bad sign, and signaling the time when you better to enter torpor for a few houndred years to survive the coming apocalypse)<br /> If you ask as a Storyteller? Similar. What and how lead to from point A (the normal, beatable character) to point B (where it is now)? But the answer is basically not important - You ARE the ST, you are responsible for the story and make it enjoyable, and if you decided, such character is not works in the chroncile, sit down with the player and talk it over.<br /> ...but if you want a solution to teach the player a lesson, eg. there is no such thing as unbeatable character, even with OP powers? As I said, such a monstorsity draws attention, and easily could end up on the top of the list of a Silverfang who <b>Paws of the Newborn Cub </b>the unliving shit out of such an anomaly (With only a glare and a snarl, the Silver Fang can temporarily suppress an opponent's supernatural tricks, leaving him to face the werewolf's wrath as nothing more than an animal or human. A falcon-spirit teaches this Gift. <i>System: The player spends two Gnosis points and rolls Gnosis (difficulty of the target's Willpower). Each success removes all supernatural powers (shapeshifting, Gifts, Disciplines, and any other sort of supernatural or magical power) from the target for one turn.)</i><br /> \u200bAnd problem solved<br /> Or simply the player's Sire or Grandsire, or anything suficiently powerfull vampire (or anyting) enough will deal with the problem <br /> Curde but effective<br /> But the most brutal of the powers is the humble Presence 3 - Entrancement<br /> Sure, you can resist presence by spending WP and roll, but the affected individual must keep spending points until he is no longer in the presence of the vampire<br /> How about 2-3 or heck, make it 5 Settite, Toreador, anything with Presence and make the ultimate, unbeatable lifeform wannabee an obidient lovestruck puppy of a fledgeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T10:20:19-07:00","id":1513089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters?p=1513083#post1513083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is damn hard to build such a PC</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't. Obtenebration and Thaumaturgy strats are all in-built to a single discipline.<br /> <br /> I mean yeah, if the players start getting to big for their boots and make too many big and threatening moves in a short space of time, there will be repercussions. Maybe they'll all get murdered in their sleep or attacked before they can do the ritual, but...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and easily could end up on the top of the list of a Silverfang who <b>Paws of the Newborn Cub </b>the unliving shit out of such an anomaly (With only a glare and a snarl, the Silver Fang can temporarily suppress an opponent's supernatural tricks, leaving him to face the werewolf's wrath as nothing more than an animal or human </div> </div> </div>...this would 100% be the storyteller being a vindictive prick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean a ST could sesne miles away, you are planning to do something like that, and to reach that combinaton of disciplines you described takes time - godd luck to have protean AND thaumaturgy on such high level </div> </div> </div>&quot;well ordinarily it wouldn't be too hard to learn this but since I know your goals I'm not going to let you reach it&quot; is not good GMing. 5 Protean, 1+ lure of flames isn't much of a stretch might I add. \u200b<br /> <br /> It's 100% reasonable for player characters to want to find methods that increase their quality of life and to not-die. It's not at all reasonable to use this as an excuse to go out of your way and make the players miserable for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-28-2023, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T11:04:53-07:00","id":1513093,"title":"","content":"But even if you are immune to physical damage, you can still be hit by a lot of other powers.<br /> In most cases fire can still damage you, and you are not immune to magic or a lot of mid altering powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T11:06:31-07:00","id":1513094,"title":"","content":"Take it as a feature.<br /> <br /> &quot;Invincible&quot; character builds are for the most part only possible by spending large portions of their XP and Freebies on things that are combat focused.<br /> <br /> Classic WOD is rarely so focused on combat that this is a major problem. Sure, your tenebrous form thaumaturge character can mow down the average ancillae, but that doesn't protect your character's friends and family if you piss off the wrong person, it doesn't prevent you from degenerating your humanity score if you go on a murder spree, and it sure as hell doesn't get your character the things they want now that they gimped their social skills to become a death machine.<br /> <br /> Honestly, &quot;Invincible&quot; characters tend to be the most vulnerable at the tables I've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T11:38:18-07:00","id":1513095,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s never came up in our games. But Prometheas has a good point that focusing into becoming a physical powerhouse comes at the cost at social and mental acumen and maybe reminding players that being a specialist comes at a great cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T12:36:44-07:00","id":1513100,"title":"","content":"There's no such a thing as an &quot;invincible character&quot; for a Storyteller. If the character is immune to physical damage, he can still be mentally assaulted/dominated/frozen in place/sent to the Abyss/or whatever, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I said, such a monstorsity draws attention, and easily could end up on the top of the list of a Silverfang who <b>Paws of the Newborn Cub </b>the unliving shit out of such an anomaly (With only a glare and a snarl, the Silver Fang can temporarily suppress an opponent's supernatural tricks, leaving him to face the werewolf's wrath as nothing more than an animal or human. A falcon-spirit teaches this Gift. <i>System: The player spends two Gnosis points and rolls Gnosis (difficulty of the target's Willpower). Each success removes all supernatural powers (shapeshifting, Gifts, Disciplines, and any other sort of supernatural or magical power) from the target for one turn.)</i>\u200b </div> </div> </div>I only have to say that this is one of the most stupid powers that the &quot;power creep&quot; era of Werewolf brought to the table (and that REALLY didn't age well), when I'm dealing with crossovers games I make what should be stated in the text of the power, that is to make it a resisted roll and then the power can be interesting. The target can resist the same way a vampire could try to resist being turned into a lawn chair.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as I said, in the end, there's no such thing as &quot;an invincible character&quot;, sooner or later &quot;someone is going to deal&quot; with him/her...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 05-28-2023, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T12:45:35-07:00","id":1513102,"title":"","content":"I would get someone else to deal with such physical powerhouses and save myself a potential beating. That\u2019s how I would handle such a problem or use Dominate, Presence and or Obfuscate to goad them into making a fatal mistake and do in themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-29-2023, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T13:32:25-07:00","id":1513106,"title":"","content":"Yet another unapproved post<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There's no such a thing as an &quot;invincible character&quot; for a Storyteller. If the character is immune to physical damage, he can still be mentally assaulted/dominated/frozen in place/sent to the Abyss/or whatever, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but if you want a solution to teach the player a lesson, eg. there is no such thing as unbeatable character, even with OP powers? As I said, such a monstorsity draws attention, and easily could end up on the top of the list of a Silverfang who <b>Paws of the Newborn Cub </b>the unliving shit out of such an anomaly (With only a glare and a snarl, the Silver Fang can temporarily suppress an opponent's supernatural tricks, leaving him to face the werewolf's wrath as nothing more than an animal or human. A falcon-spirit teaches this Gift. <i>System: The player spends two Gnosis points and rolls Gnosis (difficulty of the target's Willpower). Each success removes all supernatural powers (shapeshifting, Gifts, Disciplines, and any other sort of supernatural or magical power) from the target for one turn.)</i><br /> \u200bAnd problem solved\u200b </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I only have to say that this is one of the most stupid powers that the &quot;power creep&quot; era of Werewolf brought to the table (and that REALLY didn't age well), when I'm dealing with crossovers games I make what should be stated in the text of the power, that is to make it a resisted roll and then the power can be interesting. The target can resist the same way a vampire could try to resist being turned into a lawn chair.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as I said, in the end, there's no such thing as &quot;an invincible character&quot;, sooner or later &quot;someone is going to deal&quot; with him/her...\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T14:27:32-07:00","id":1513113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters?p=1513094#post1513094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, &quot;Invincible&quot; characters tend to be the most vulnerable at the tables I've seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>You must have a great ST (congrats if that is you) at your table and good players at the table.<br /> <br /> While I agree with everything you say in principle, in practice I've seen combat oriented characters often take over the game and dominate the other PCs. It takes a skilled ST to handle them and create the situations you describe. (Or to increase the stakes / change the story for them because they get noticed by more powerful vampires who can use such pawns or want to eliminate such a threat.) Then if such a ST does exist and is able to handle that PC so it is not unbalancing for the game, often the player of the unkillable combat monster throws a hissy fit and makes things uncomfortable for everyone else at the table. It leaves a bad taste in everyone's mouth even if that player later leaves.<br /> <br /> In my experience, the players who want to build the unkillable combat monster do not take &quot;losing&quot; in such ways gracefully and typically want to burn everything down with them. They don't tend to be the mature players. So players who do build such PCs (for whatever reason), yet accept any bad consequences from their lack of other useful skills and does not turn every conflict into &quot;kill them all&quot;, are very rare.<br /> <br /> I don't have this kind of problem now with my gaming groups, but I had to churn through a good number of them when I was an early VtM gamer.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typos 05-31-2023, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T15:16:49-07:00","id":1513122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters?p=1513106#post1513106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet another unapproved post<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There's no such a thing as an &quot;invincible character&quot; for a Storyteller. If the character is immune to physical damage, he can still be mentally assaulted/dominated/frozen in place/sent to the Abyss/or whatever, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To be fair, I only have to say that this is one of the most stupid powers that the &quot;power creep&quot; era of Werewolf brought to the table (and that REALLY didn't age well), when I'm dealing with crossovers games I make what should be stated in the text of the power, that is to make it a resisted roll and then the power can be interesting. The target can resist the same way a vampire could try to resist being turned into a lawn chair.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as I said, in the end, there's no such thing as &quot;an invincible character&quot;, sooner or later &quot;someone is going to deal&quot; with him/her...\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So... your definition of the &quot;power creep&quot; era of Werewolf is Werewolf, since Paws of the Newborn Cub has been there since 1992 (and it does incorporate passive resistance of a sort; if you're crabby with that, maybe consider the mechanics of Dominate.)<br /> <br /> This plainly isn't power creep, though, but an altogether different game. The game in question happens to be highly focused on splatter instead of personal horror, and in splatter, there's a high chance of characters not getting to experience meaningful degeneration because a throwback fomor tore them in half, or at substantially more epic levels of danger, an irradiated Zmei exhaled nuclear fire onto them and they were utterly disintegrated. And rather than just hide and avoid these dangers, the Garou and Fera are obligated to find a solution to them, which for the Garou typically means fights and, one hopes, battles better thought out than just frontal assaults. PotNC helps to provide a bit of added survivability, but given how high the difficulty is likely to be, it's far from a sure shot; the same holds for most Gifts on par with it, like Kiss of Helios or Luna's Avenger. Those are rather late-game powers, though, not really something that a min maxer can sink a bunch of Discipline points into and just start out with, for the most part - some patron spirits can grant Rank 5 Gifts, but that also basically increases the heat on the pack, since having Katanka-Sonnak/Hyperion, an incarna under Helios representing the physical sun, is all kinds of rare, incredibly momentous, and also saddles the pack with an obligation to push back against the Garou Nation party line on the War of Rage and actively aid Fera in trouble. Note that the other two Gifts named are not available in this fashion; the Silver Fangs are not nearly so cavalier in sharing their greatest powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T18:35:24-07:00","id":1513143,"title":"","content":"I deal with invincible characters out-of-character by talking to the player and figuring out what they want from the experience, explaining what I want from the experience, explaining how they might be disrupting other people's fun, and trying to come to a resolution. Mechanical tricks and tactical sleights-of-hand are fun, definitely, but they absolutely need to seem like natural outcroppings of the plot and not vindictive lightning bolts from above.<br /> <br /> I say this because the power balance in Vampire (and especially other WoD splats) is more an out-of-character thing than an in-character thing, more a meta-idea than one codified by the system itself. The books have never been shy about telling the players that they're going to be crushed and that they're always going to be weaker and This Isn't D&amp;D, What Do You Mean You Want the Cool Powers, Fuck Off. The power balance is meta because since the books encourage a less-empowered player experience and a more &quot;heavy-handed&quot; ST approach (as opposed to a &quot;challenge rating&quot; system-based approach), when the ST takes a heavy hand, that hand can take many forms. Often, it takes the form of some unfairness (to be fair, this could be real or perceived unfairness), and then the true balance of the game is revealed: the ST controls what happens <i>at the table</i>. The Players control whether they are <b><i>at</i></b> the table. If they don't like how the ST balances the game, things change drastically in terms of power balancing when they realize they can walk.<br /> <br /> All of a sudden, sure, Elder McFuckOff killed Jim's hypersoldier, but now Jim's gone and he ain't coming back anytime soon and the nearest replacement is two states over, or is on a server so now we're playing at least semi-remotely instead of in-person and using dice bots, or can't make our usual schedule for whatever reason, or is a much bigger asshole, or wants to play a different tone of game, or will not stop hitting on the female players...you get the idea. So either the ST makes concessions to replace their player (and the incoming player gets to learn exactly why a spot's open), or the party is now a vamp down - and while The Game's Not About Combat, sure, it's still bad to be down a whole character's worth of disciplines, skills, connections, and abilities, even if they were 90-100% &quot;kill anything that moves&quot;. Suddenly your new party of Party minus Jim is in this world where either Elder McFuckOff just vanishes and doesn't punish Jim's known associates, indicating that they were a targeted strike on Jim's ego, or Elder McFuckOff <i>does</i> stick around and puts their boot on the remaining PCs' necks, in which case they probably saw Jim walk out the door and are wondering if they can make it through before traffic backs up. That's not even taking into account whether or not Jim owns the house everyone plays at, who drives whom, who <b><i>lives with </i></b>whom, who brings the tasty snacks to sessions...there's a lot of out-of-character politics that can very quickly come into play.<br /> <br /> Just talk to them. Good players are as rare as Salubri - treasure them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27305-joanna_crone","name":"Joanna_Crone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T19:10:32-07:00","id":1513148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters?p=1513113#post1513113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You must have a great ST (congrats if that is you) at your table and good players at the table.<br /> <br /> While I agree with everything you say in principle, in practice I've seen combat oriented characters often take over the game and dominate the other PCs. It takes a skilled ST to handle them and create the situations you describe. (Or to increase the stakes / change the story for them because they get noticed by more powerful vampires who can use such pawns or want to eliminate such a threat.) Then if such a ST does exist and is able to handle that PC so it is not unbalancing for the game, often the player of the unkillable combat monster throws a hissy fit and makes things uncomfortable for everyone else at the table. It leaves a bad taste in everyone's mouth even if that player later leaves.<br /> <br /> In my experience, the players who want to build the unkillable combat monster do not take &quot;losing&quot; in such ways gracefully and typically want to burn everything down with them. They don't tend to be the mature players. So players who do build such PCs (for whatever reason), yet accept any bad consequences from their lack of other useful skills and does not turn every conflict into &quot;kill them all&quot;, are very rare.<br /> <br /> I don't have this kind of problem now with my gaming groups, but I had to churn throw a good number of them when I was an early VtM gamer.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So this was my experience exactly, and believe I talked about this in an old post. Not all the D&amp;D type players were able to make the switch. There were two combat junkies who wanted combat, combat, combat. One player felt the need to kill off party members as normal weekly activity. If a player puts everything into combat and you are playing even a bit more powerful vampires the player who didn't really stands no chance. If a player decides he wants to kill fellow players it's really not that hard. What is the point of letting people who think it's roll-playing instead of role-playing wreck all the work you put into chronicles on a regular basis?<br /> <br /> The best thing to do is drop the players who don't fit in your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T00:06:07-07:00","id":1513169,"title":"","content":"Here' my problem though<br /> I'm not talking about psychotic powergamers, I'm talking about characters that can smash through parts of the story if you give them some time to prep. You can be 'invincible' in the combat sense while investing relatively little and instead focusing on your socials/mentals/virtues/willpower.\u200b That's probably the case in most of the examples given, since as a thaumaturge you want to be mental/willpower heavy and most kinds don't really need physicals while an Obtenebration user wants at least high manipulation.<br /> <br /> <b>Perfectly viable starter character only using things from 20th core and not using merits</b>:<br /> <br /> Attributes<br /> 2/2/2, 2/4/2, 2/4/4<br /> <br /> Skills: Do whatever makes you a fully fleshed out character. Occult 4<br /> <br /> Backgrounds: Doesn't matter. I'd go for mentor, allies or domain mostly. <br /> <br /> Disciplines:<br /> Thaumaturgy 3 (You'll probably want 4 depending on path, 7 freebies)<br /> some Good choices: Blood (4) lure of flames (3) Movement of the mind (3) Elements (4, but I'd stat myself differently for this one)<br /> <br /> rituals<br /> 1- doesn't matter<br /> 2- smoke. Warding circles are also great. <br /> 3-incorporeal passage. (though clinging of the insect is quite fun to abuse too) <b>Pavis of foul Presence</b> will deflect a number of single target presence skills.<br /> 4- doesn't matter<br /> <br /> Freebies:<br /> 5 on willpower<br /> 7 on an extra thaumaturgy level<br /> 2 on more occult. <br /> 1 on whatever, go get some flaws for more. <br /> <br /> <br /> Like, you're not stretching at all to build this guy at character creation. He or she could be a delightful addition to the team... I'd probably buy some Auspex later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T06:02:26-07:00","id":1513190,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> <br /> <br /> You remind me how much I dislike Thaumaturgy for Vampires <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I don't want to look all that up.<br /> <br /> Let's just pretend you said Obtenebration 5 instead, or Protean 5 or Obfuscate 5, or Dominate 3 really. These choices will trivialize a good chunk of encounters in there own way and can be used as a starting character. I would suggest you insist on a little creativity from session to session. If it is a player that just sweeps the leg in street fighter the whole time is he really having fun after awhile? I don't think most players will get upset if you hit him with a well thought out counter from an opponent. Players like to be challenged.<br /> <br /> Doing the same thing over and over again will become noticed if it directed at fellow Kindred or even Ghouls. Those in power who are losing allies will look at the victims, sus out motivations and who is benefitting. Figure out who not only had motive, but the ability to pull it off. They will use disciplines themselves to unmask their opponents.<br /> <br /> If they keep taking out fellow vampires it will be noticed probably sooner rather than later and people will deal with the problem. It's pretty easy for an NPC to kill a player with a little prep time as well.<br /> <br /> I was going to say set the story up as a mystery or matter of diplomacy and bargaining, but I'm sure you already do various scenarios. If the players go too solution is to kill his fellow vampires they can't really complain when they meet a sticky end. Violence begets violence and all that. If their character is killed for taking out several people in an organization, they might think of other ways to do things next time. Call it a learning experience. Hacking the game to kill others with &quot;prep time&quot; does not make you powerful enough to fend off the consequences of your actions if they piss off the wrong people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T06:58:18-07:00","id":1513193,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it a little more.<br /> <br /> If a player kills a low level vampire through a clever tactic who cares, but if say 4 vampires get taken out in as many months, the Prince will be highly motivated to find out who's doing it. The right of destruction is the Princes for a reason. He can't have a loose cannon killing Kindred indiscriminately for his own safety and power structure that will weaken if the Prince is seen as someone who's lost control of the city. I'd say if he and the hound couldn't get to the bottom of it he would call in an Archon to see what was going on. It's one of the reasons the Camarilla works.<br /> <br /> If these are humans, Vampires kill humans. The players may still be making enemies depending on the target, but if you want to drop all your points in say Celerity where you dodge their one action then take your other 5 for insta death it probably wont be a death sentence from on high. Humans are food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T15:31:27-07:00","id":1513241,"title":"","content":"Invulnerable PCs is a side effect of the &quot;white room&quot; mentality. <br /> <br /> Someone looks at some groups of mechanics and realizes you can put them together to form a new interaction. The issue is that they are often thinking of only one situation. Such as direct face to face combat, but that falls apart if the opponent is using a different approach.<br /> <br /> Protean 2 / Celerity 5 / Potence 5 means pretty much anything nearby is shredded, so you use a sniper who is about a mile away. If someone is a lower generation level than you and has Dominate, then you only interact with them via phone calls. If someone has a lot of influence over the city, then you destroy the lives of every mortal that owes them a favor or allegiance.<br /> <br /> Even if a character is largely unkillable, it doesn't mean that they can't be hurt or their interests can't be messed with. Furthermore, such unkillable characters are not omniscient so if you are doing something against them, unless you are very sloppy, there is no way to know who is attacking their interests or powerbase. Finally, they can't be everywhere at once, meaning that if they decide to protect a given thing or person, they can't be everywhere else.<br /> <br /> So yeah, you might not be able to kill them in a head to head fight, but you can destroy every mortal connection they have, destroy their havens, crash their businesses, and decimate their influence. Eventually they will either move on to greener pastures or they will get isolated enough that someone from their past might see an opportunity to take them out and they might have a way around the invulnerable combo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T15:47:21-07:00","id":1513244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters#post1513057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So some combinations of powers make individuals virtually unkillable and yet they remain super dangerous. How do you deal with that? </div> </div> </div> </div>Characters with strong and definitive protection, avoidence, resistance, or evasion qualities or powers can still be challanged socially or through the use of environment. Especially if they are separated from their supporters, followers, or allies.<br /> Research, scouting, or espionage can be used to find out what sort of physical upgrade or mystical protection will be used by an opponent. Standard tactics like use of extensive resources, planned preparation, and creating distractions can still be relevant. <br /> Vampires using the mentioned powers or abilities can still be challanged directly by dedicated specialist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T22:02:56-07:00","id":1513264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters?p=1513241#post1513241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> So yeah, you might not be able to kill them in a head to head fight, but you can destroy every mortal connection they have, destroy their havens, crash their businesses, and decimate their influence. Eventually they will either move on to greener pastures or they will get isolated enough that someone from their past might see an opportunity to take them out and they might have a way around the invulnerable combo.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems a whiter &quot;white room&quot; compared to building a specific &quot;invulnerability combo&quot; with only internal constraints (you have to just buy discipline not go around destroying the city).<br /> If the NPC goes on a killing spree there should be a setting response other than the character response. If there are no consequences for the NPC action you are killing not only the character's mortal/vampiric contacts but also the suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> The &quot;invincible combos&quot; are a problem because the system does not provide any instrument to both player and storyteller to handle them in a sane non-competitive way. And it does not matter if the book says &quot;We are not D&amp;D&quot; a thousand times because the rule as written does not support any game style more complex than dungeon-less dungeon crawling without a strong intervention of the Storyteller. Also for a game of personal horror the ratio between introspection mechanics and fight mechanics is definitely too low. In general, the ratio between any non-combat-related mechanics and combat-related mechanics is too low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T23:54:38-07:00","id":1513268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters?p=1513264#post1513264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems a whiter &quot;white room&quot; compared to building a specific &quot;invulnerability combo&quot; with only internal constraints (you have to just buy discipline not go around destroying the city).<br /> If the NPC goes on a killing spree there should be a setting response other than the character response. If there are no consequences for the NPC action you are killing not only the character's mortal/vampiric contacts but also the suspension of disbelief.</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition a &quot;White Room&quot; lacks the ramifications of any surroundings, settings, environment, or in the case of VtM usually forgets about the interactions with things like Backgrounds and alternate playstyles. So how is suggesting that an invulnerable combo could be defeated by using these other mechanics and play options a &quot;whiter&quot; white room?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters?p=1513264#post1513264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;invincible combos&quot; are a problem because the system does not provide any instrument to both player and storyteller to handle them in a sane non-competitive way. And it does not matter if the book says &quot;We are not D&amp;D&quot; a thousand times because the rule as written does not support any game style more complex than dungeon-less dungeon crawling without a strong intervention of the Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly are you complaining about? If everything is auto-balanced mechanically, then everything is in a permanent stalemate. The game of chess is balanced in the numbers of pieces each player has and the limited number of spaces on the board. Conversely a game like Poker has static values of the cards, but your ability to bluff (roleplay) and the size of your chip stack varies from play to play creating a dynamic game environment. In short, imbalance can often create the fun people are looking for in a &quot;balanced game&quot;. Game design is weird like that.<br /> <br /> If any game system is descending into a Dungeon Crawl with no greater depth than kill everything and take their stuff... then either that is exactly what the group is wanting or the group lacks bigger ideas of game play. I have lost track of the number of D&amp;D games I have played where the majority of game play was composed of non-murder hobo activities. Game mechanics are just tools and ingredients, how you use them matters, just like in cooking. <br /> <br /> Try building a game around using &amp; building Backgrounds rather than Disciplines as your main way of getting things done and you will see what I am talking about. You will have to completely rethink how you approach encounters, how you tell stories, how you create tension, and all of that without actually changing a single rule or mechanic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513057-how-do-you-deal-with-invincible-characters?p=1513264#post1513264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also for a game of personal horror the ratio between introspection mechanics and fight mechanics is definitely too low. In general, the ratio between any non-combat-related mechanics and combat-related mechanics is too low.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will agree that many of the Background systems are woefully underdeveloped if you have ambitions for something more than street coterie level games. But the core issue with your statement is that &quot;personal horror&quot; can't be codified in anything but the broadest of strokes. It is on the ST and Players to make the game personal horror or whatever else they want it to be.<br /> <br /> Regrettably there is a key problem with non-combat mechanics, the People themselves. Specifically, if a Player isn't well versed in say science, yes they could play a Chemist, but they wouldn't know what they could do with that knowledge. The ST could try to have the player roll and then inform the Player that they had an idea, but once again the ST has to have knowledge of chemistry to suggest what could be done.<br /> <br /> In essence everyone knows that you can kick or punch, the mechanics just manage the interaction, but non-combat skills often require a degree of extra knowledge or inspiration to make work, but mechanics can't do that for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T22:56:04-07:00","id":1513360,"title":"","content":"As you say &quot;white room&quot; scenario is in a general sense a scenario planned or studied without considering the context, your suggestion that you can destroy anything other than the character itself lacks any consideration for the surroundings and does not contain any reference to the settings.<br /> If you consider a character with five dots of Obtenebration and abyssal mysticism a &quot;white room&quot; scenario then destroying everything seems definitely a whiter room scenario to me.<br /> <br /> Poker is far way more balanced than the vast majority of RPGs, at least we all draw the cards from the same deck.<br /> <br /> Have you ever tried to read a game that actually has a significant collection of mechanics for something outside of combat or a game with narrative mechanics? They offer plenty of game opportunities outside of combats without the additional effort of building a game that focuses on Backgrounds when the rule set is almost entirely devoted to Disciplines. Mechanics help to convert players' ideas into game events, the fastest way to have Background relevant in the chronicle is to have mechanics that make them directly usable by the players without additional work or intervention from the storyteller.<br /> <br /> And as you noted in the last part of your post, the problem is that people do not know what they can do with the dots on their character sheet. Providing them with specific mechanics helps to lessen this problem. If anyone knows that you can kick and punch maybe the rule of the game should provide more guidance for the rest of the thighs that you can do during play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}